# MOS Persistent Cognitive Substrate (PCS)

# Specification v0.1

# Part VI — PostgreSQL Reference Implementation

---

# Abstract

This document defines the PostgreSQL reference implementation of the Memory Operating System Persistent Cognitive Substrate.

The purpose of this implementation is not to make PostgreSQL the required database engine for MOS.

Instead, PostgreSQL serves as the first complete implementation demonstrating that the PCS specification can be realized using mature database technologies.

This reference implementation provides:

* relational persistence,
* graph capabilities,
* vector search,
* temporal storage,
* event processing,
* provenance tracking,
* version management,
* distributed operation.

---

# Chapter 1

# Implementation Philosophy

The PostgreSQL implementation follows one core rule:

> The database stores cognitive truth. Derived systems accelerate access to that truth.

Therefore:

Authoritative:

* entities,
* facts,
* events,
* relationships,
* versions,
* provenance.

Derived:

* embeddings,
* caches,
* summaries,
* indexes,
* projections.

Derived data may be rebuilt.

Authoritative data may not be lost.

